WEBVTT

00:00:08.333 --> 00:00:10.750
"Spear of Heaven."

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:13.083
"Shield of Earth."

00:00:13.083 --> 00:00:18.542
The government had gone forward
with their final plan to bury Koro Sensei.

00:00:18.542 --> 00:00:22.375
We couldn't get them to hear us out.

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:28.417
Our last mission: get everyone to school safely!

00:00:28.417 --> 00:00:30.917
We need to see him.

00:00:30.917 --> 00:00:33.708
This won't end unless we do.

00:00:34.542 --> 00:00:36.958
Countdown to Koro Sensei's dead-line:

00:00:36.958 --> 00:00:39.125
three hours!

00:00:45.417 --> 00:00:47.833
<i>"Wait, just hang on a sec!"</i>

00:00:47.833 --> 00:00:50.833
<i>I scream, but it gets me nowhere</i>

00:00:50.833 --> 00:00:53.292
<i>I put all my strength into being afraid of</i>

00:00:53.292 --> 00:00:56.083
<i>The limits that just kept on closing in</i>

00:00:56.083 --> 00:00:58.625
<i>Reality is merciless</i>

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:01.333
<i>And time is especially tricky</i>

00:01:01.333 --> 00:01:06.583
<i>It's like someone's snatching away</i>
<i>the blanket I just can't sleep without</i>

00:01:06.583 --> 00:01:12.708
<i>We laughed and fretted</i>

00:01:12.708 --> 00:01:17.250
<i>Over silly things, nonsensical things</i>

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:23.375
<i>Once the final bell rings out</i>

00:01:23.375 --> 00:01:27.958
<i>The fun times will be over, too</i>

00:01:27.958 --> 00:01:29.500
<i>Bye-bye, yesterday</i>

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:35.500
<i>365 days' worth of lessons shoved into bags</i>

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:38.583
<i>Like always, like it's "see you tomorrow"</i>

00:01:38.583 --> 00:01:40.125
<i>Bye-bye, yesterday</i>

00:01:40.125 --> 00:01:44.208
<i>365 days' worth of happenings</i>

00:01:44.208 --> 00:01:49.208
<i>If you've made me an adult,</i>
<i>don't be showing me tears</i>

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:50.708
<i>Bye-bye, yesterday</i>

00:01:50.708 --> 00:01:52.208
<i>365 days' worth of memories</i>

00:01:52.208 --> 00:01:54.833
"3 Hours Till Koro Sensei's Dead-Line"
<i>365 days' worth of memories</i>

00:01:54.833 --> 00:01:57.333
<i>Even if I grow up some more</i>

00:01:57.333 --> 00:02:00.167
<i>They still won't fade a bit</i>

00:02:09.958 --> 00:02:13.958
"22nd Period: Happy Birthday Time"
"by Yukiko Kanzaki & Rio Nakamura"

00:02:20.958 --> 00:02:24.792
Three hours until the
Spear of Heaven is fully charged.

00:02:24.792 --> 00:02:28.417
Shame we'll be destroying him so completely;

00:02:28.417 --> 00:02:30.583
what a waste of rare test samples.

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:33.500
All in the name of world peace...

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:36.792
Can those kids make it through?

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:39.500
What is it?!

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:41.042
An intruder on the mountain!

00:02:41.042 --> 00:02:43.583
Seems they've gotten past the police line!

00:02:46.083 --> 00:02:48.125
I-It's a mob of monsters!

00:02:51.792 --> 00:02:53.042
What a nightmare!

00:02:53.042 --> 00:02:55.042
I can't tell how many there are!

00:02:55.042 --> 00:02:57.208
Think you can mess with us?

00:03:02.292 --> 00:03:03.667
Okay...

00:03:03.667 --> 00:03:06.250
Nice teamwork, you three.

00:03:07.333 --> 00:03:10.083
We've lost communication with the B squad.

00:03:10.083 --> 00:03:12.917
This intruder must be
the real deal. Watch yourself.

00:03:12.917 --> 00:03:14.333
Got it.

00:03:18.292 --> 00:03:19.750
H-Hey!

00:03:21.292 --> 00:03:25.208
A sniper--and they've spotted us all! Location--

00:03:27.625 --> 00:03:30.833
Hey, uh... that didn't sound so great.

00:03:30.833 --> 00:03:32.042
He's fine.

00:03:32.042 --> 00:03:34.375
I wrapped him up nice and soft, that's all.

00:03:34.375 --> 00:03:36.833
This squad's taken care of, Karma.

00:03:36.833 --> 00:03:38.375
Okay.

00:03:38.375 --> 00:03:39.792
How's things by you?

00:03:39.792 --> 00:03:41.958
Hmm? Right now...

00:03:41.958 --> 00:03:42.042
Agh! Hot! It burns!

00:03:42.042 --> 00:03:44.625
"Wasabi"
Agh! Hot! It burns!

00:03:44.625 --> 00:03:47.792
--Ow! It burns!
--Sorry 'bout that! But you're all such <i>pros</i>.

00:03:47.792 --> 00:03:51.208
How else am I going to get you to scream?

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:55.917
Your screams'll be the bait
to lure even more reinforcements.

00:03:55.917 --> 00:03:59.250
I'd like to take care of
two or three more while I'm here.

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:01.000
That's doable, right, Ritsu?

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.167
Yes...

00:04:02.167 --> 00:04:05.333
About three more
are approaching over the ridge.

00:04:05.333 --> 00:04:07.333
And there's a fixed machine gun

00:04:07.333 --> 00:04:09.375
on the high ground, with all the fir trees.

00:04:09.375 --> 00:04:10.750
Roger.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.750
So if we go from the crimson-glory-vine thicket

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:14.792
through the stand of stone oaks?

00:04:14.792 --> 00:04:17.542
Yep, that should get you there.

00:04:17.542 --> 00:04:20.542
Okay, Terasaka, go that way,
take down their guys,

00:04:20.542 --> 00:04:22.417
and advance to the lone pine.

00:04:22.417 --> 00:04:23.833
Got it!

00:04:34.458 --> 00:04:36.125
Squads C and D have gone missing!

00:04:36.125 --> 00:04:37.542
I need a status report, pronto!

00:04:37.542 --> 00:04:40.708
What's the meaning of this, Karasuma?!

00:04:40.708 --> 00:04:44.208
That mountain is those students' home turf.

00:04:44.208 --> 00:04:47.417
They've spent the last year there
going after a super-creature,

00:04:47.417 --> 00:04:51.167
having fun, and taking classes.

00:04:51.167 --> 00:04:54.167
They'll know their way around it
blindfolded by now.

00:04:54.167 --> 00:04:56.500
Right there, on that patch of campus,

00:04:56.500 --> 00:05:00.083
they're the world's most terrifying assassins.

00:05:00.083 --> 00:05:02.208
Were you behind all this?

00:05:02.208 --> 00:05:05.917
They made their own decision.
They formed their own plan.

00:05:05.917 --> 00:05:08.375
And they carried it out themselves.

00:05:08.375 --> 00:05:11.333
Even if we tried to hold them back,

00:05:11.333 --> 00:05:14.083
they'd be ready to bust through
with everything they've got.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:17.417
Like a proud papa.

00:05:18.792 --> 00:05:21.208
Okajima, I'm there.

00:05:21.208 --> 00:05:23.583
Another fifty meters.

00:05:23.583 --> 00:05:27.875
Karma Akabane'd be
most suited to take command.

00:05:27.875 --> 00:05:31.792
With his devilish brain, he'll use
anything and everything at his disposal.

00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:34.417
What the--?!

00:05:34.417 --> 00:05:36.542
How many of 'em <i>are </i>there?!

00:05:42.292 --> 00:05:45.000
We're just gonna zap you a little, 'kay?

00:05:47.125 --> 00:05:50.167
This mountain's just <i>covered </i>with traps.

00:05:50.167 --> 00:05:53.750
Even if we <i>did </i>set 'em for Koro Sensei.

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:58.458
Hey! Lemme down!

00:06:09.542 --> 00:06:10.500
Tch!

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:13.250
Still some o' you jokers left, eh?

00:06:14.042 --> 00:06:17.000
It's true: we did let our guard down.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:20.750
Looks like you kids are far better
at this place than we are.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:26.000
Stun darts, eh?

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:28.083
But if you know what you're up against...

00:06:28.083 --> 00:06:30.583
...it's no problem at all.

00:06:40.125 --> 00:06:41.542
Karma!

00:06:42.208 --> 00:06:43.833
You punks...

00:06:43.833 --> 00:06:48.167
If you'd only behave, this'd all be over.

00:06:48.167 --> 00:06:52.417
What in blazes are you
objecting to this late in the game?!

00:06:52.417 --> 00:06:55.458
This is something we have to resolve ourselves!

00:06:55.458 --> 00:06:58.917
You don't get to march in now
and boss us around!

00:07:00.875 --> 00:07:03.583
Please trust us on the whole Koro Sensei thing!

00:07:03.583 --> 00:07:06.833
Just let us handle it already!

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:14.667
Karma!

00:07:24.542 --> 00:07:26.333
Nagisa?

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:32.292
Hey! He's still moving!

00:07:32.292 --> 00:07:34.625
You damn brats!

00:07:34.625 --> 00:07:36.917
Finish him off right, you dumbasses!

00:07:36.917 --> 00:07:40.125
You can keep your show-off high-fives!

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:44.125
There's no response from any of our troops!

00:07:44.125 --> 00:07:45.417
What?!

00:07:54.292 --> 00:07:57.292
I could tell by the sound.

00:07:57.292 --> 00:07:59.042
Sir...

00:07:59.042 --> 00:08:03.458
You've come so far, class.

00:08:03.458 --> 00:08:05.667
Koro Sensei!

00:08:10.167 --> 00:08:14.208
You mean those students crossed
the barrier fully aware of the danger?

00:08:14.208 --> 00:08:17.125
What could that possibly accomplish?!

00:08:17.125 --> 00:08:20.333
They're civilians--we can't
leave them to their own devices.

00:08:20.333 --> 00:08:26.083
It could be catastrophic
if the cornered target gets desperate.

00:08:26.083 --> 00:08:30.875
Irina and I will go. We can talk them down.

00:08:30.875 --> 00:08:32.292
Bleah.

00:08:34.792 --> 00:08:37.583
That's the light from the laser...

00:08:37.583 --> 00:08:44.417
I see. So they'll be firing
the killing laser just before midnight.

00:08:44.417 --> 00:08:49.375
That much power would even
shut down my Absolute Defense Form.

00:08:49.375 --> 00:08:50.625
No!

00:08:50.625 --> 00:08:53.375
Koro Sensei, let's find a way out of here!

00:08:53.375 --> 00:08:57.000
We'll be your hostages--or whatever it takes!

00:08:58.208 --> 00:09:02.000
There's no stopping that laser now,

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:06.333
not when people know I'm out there.

00:09:06.333 --> 00:09:10.250
Did you know all along
that it would come to this?

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:12.833
Even if I don't explode,

00:09:12.833 --> 00:09:17.583
you can't expect all these nations
not to be afraid of a creature like me.

00:09:17.583 --> 00:09:19.875
Sooner or later, they'll want to snuff me out.

00:09:19.875 --> 00:09:22.875
It's only reasonable.

00:09:24.083 --> 00:09:28.083
There might have been a way
if only we'd acted sooner...

00:09:28.083 --> 00:09:30.417
Like breaking the barrier projectors,

00:09:30.417 --> 00:09:31.708
"Octo-Creature's Students' Tearful Appeal!"
or making the rounds online and on TV to plead our case!

00:09:31.708 --> 00:09:33.583
or making the rounds online and on TV to plead our case!

00:09:33.583 --> 00:09:37.542
That would have gotten you
labeled even more dangerous,

00:09:37.542 --> 00:09:41.000
and you might have been placed
under stricter surveillance.

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:44.667
Besides, the projectors
have impregnable defenses.

00:09:44.667 --> 00:09:46.917
There are anti-aircraft weapons in place

00:09:46.917 --> 00:09:49.958
if I so much as huck a rock at them.

00:09:49.958 --> 00:09:52.208
With your current capabilities and equipment,

00:09:52.208 --> 00:09:54.833
you'd likely get caught along the way.

00:09:54.833 --> 00:09:58.583
<i>That </i>is how perfect this plan was.

00:09:58.583 --> 00:10:02.875
They spared nothing,
pouring in tech and time and people.

00:10:02.875 --> 00:10:04.333
This assassination,

00:10:04.333 --> 00:10:06.750
this crystallization of
the world's wisdom and efforts,

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:10.833
surpasses my own abilities,
for which I offer my respect

00:10:10.833 --> 00:10:15.417
and am honored to have been its target.

00:10:16.708 --> 00:10:21.583
But... Then all our hard work
getting here--that was all wasted?

00:10:21.583 --> 00:10:25.750
Is anything ever really wasted, Yada?

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:28.708
You went all the way to space to find out

00:10:28.708 --> 00:10:34.083
that the probability of
my exploding was less than 1 percent.

00:10:34.083 --> 00:10:38.375
That brought the light back
to a darkly sinking E Class,

00:10:38.375 --> 00:10:43.083
and the month that followed
was short, but very sweet.

00:10:44.125 --> 00:10:48.583
That process, your hearts--
that's what's important.

00:10:48.583 --> 00:10:53.542
You used every last bit
of what you learned to come see me.

00:10:53.542 --> 00:10:58.333
As a teacher,
there can be no greater happiness.

00:10:58.333 --> 00:11:01.917
So what if time's up?

00:11:01.917 --> 00:11:07.208
It's just 1 percent!
That's a risk we'll take--and gladly!

00:11:07.208 --> 00:11:10.083
Why won't the government
and the rest of 'em hear us out,

00:11:10.083 --> 00:11:12.458
when we're the ones
who've been closest to you?

00:11:12.458 --> 00:11:16.375
This octopus... okay, he's a perv,
but he's not <i>dangerous</i>!

00:11:16.375 --> 00:11:19.042
"We won't listen to
what those kids have to say.

00:11:19.042 --> 00:11:21.667
We'll just pity them instead."

00:11:21.667 --> 00:11:23.125
It's insulting.

00:11:23.125 --> 00:11:25.375
Like we can shut up and take this...

00:11:25.375 --> 00:11:28.333
Next time I see those goons, I'm gonna--

00:11:30.458 --> 00:11:36.333
Terasaka, all of you...
Let me give you some advice.

00:11:36.333 --> 00:11:38.458
As you go through life,

00:11:38.458 --> 00:11:41.208
the mighty current of society
is bound to get in your way,

00:11:41.208 --> 00:11:44.708
and there will certainly be times
things don't go as you'd hoped.

00:11:44.708 --> 00:11:49.292
When this happens,
do not look to society for a cause.

00:11:49.292 --> 00:11:52.625
Do not renounce society.

00:11:52.625 --> 00:11:57.208
Frankly, you'd be wasting your time.

00:11:57.208 --> 00:12:00.875
Instead, just say, "That's life!"

00:12:00.875 --> 00:12:04.167
and muddle your way through with frustration.

00:12:04.167 --> 00:12:06.958
Once you're past it, consider:

00:12:06.958 --> 00:12:10.000
If society's swift current
is tossing you around,

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:14.250
how should you
be swimming there in its midst?

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:18.250
You should have learned how,
here in the E Class,

00:12:18.250 --> 00:12:20.875
in this assassination classroom.

00:12:20.875 --> 00:12:24.250
You don't always have to
stand and face it head-on.

00:12:24.250 --> 00:12:26.958
You can run, and you can hide.

00:12:26.958 --> 00:12:30.083
If it's not against the rules,
you can try a sneak attack.

00:12:30.083 --> 00:12:33.667
You can use unconventional weapons.

00:12:33.667 --> 00:12:36.667
Stay determined--
not impatient nor discouraged--

00:12:36.667 --> 00:12:38.750
and with repeated trial and error,

00:12:38.750 --> 00:12:42.458
you're bound to reach
a splendid outcome eventually.

00:12:42.458 --> 00:12:46.000
That's because each and every
one of you is a top-tier assassin

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:49.292
who can do just that.

00:12:49.292 --> 00:12:52.708
Geez. A lesson, really? Now?

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:57.083
Now's the time for this lesson.

00:12:57.083 --> 00:13:02.083
An educator never misses
an opportunity to teach.

00:13:02.083 --> 00:13:07.792
But you know, for you to try
so whole-heartedly to save me...

00:13:07.792 --> 00:13:11.875
I'm so happy, I've been
holding back tears this whole time.

00:13:11.875 --> 00:13:14.083
I mean it.

00:13:16.708 --> 00:13:21.792
How can Koro Sensei be so calm?

00:13:21.792 --> 00:13:23.833
If he hadn't come to our E Class,

00:13:23.833 --> 00:13:28.333
he might've been able
to live a normal life somewhere.

00:13:28.333 --> 00:13:32.375
We were Koro Sensei's...

00:13:33.667 --> 00:13:35.500
By the way, Nakamura,

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:39.458
your footsteps were awfully gentle,
even during that pitched battle.

00:13:39.458 --> 00:13:43.000
And... do I smell something sweet?

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:45.833
Sharp ears <i>and </i>a sharp nose...

00:13:45.833 --> 00:13:49.625
It's been exactly one year
since the day the moon exploded, right?

00:13:49.625 --> 00:13:54.917
As I recall, Miss Yukimura
made today your birthday.

00:13:54.917 --> 00:13:59.167
Feel free to praise my skill
in getting this here in one p--

00:13:59.167 --> 00:14:00.125
Hey! I'm <i>talking</i>!

00:14:00.125 --> 00:14:02.250
But... it's just...

00:14:02.250 --> 00:14:04.542
It's my first sweet <i>anything </i>in a week!

00:14:04.542 --> 00:14:09.708
Ew, you're drooling!
Come on, guys--let's get singing!

00:14:09.708 --> 00:14:11.125
And... go!

00:14:11.125 --> 00:14:15.375
♪ Happy birthday to you, ♪

00:14:15.375 --> 00:14:19.542
--Man, this is some bullshit--tooo youuu!
--♪ happy birthday to you! ♪

00:14:19.542 --> 00:14:26.333
♪ Happy birthday, dear Koro Sensei... ♪

00:14:26.333 --> 00:14:34.333
♪ Happy birthday to you! ♪

00:14:34.333 --> 00:14:35.917
This is more than enough.

00:14:35.917 --> 00:14:38.000
C'mon, blow it out, Koro Sensei!

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:42.708
--A far greater reward than I deserve.
--There's just one, so make it count!

00:14:55.583 --> 00:14:58.000
Happy birthday.

00:15:00.292 --> 00:15:02.125
Shi--no!

00:15:02.125 --> 00:15:03.833
Yanagisawa...

00:15:03.833 --> 00:15:05.708
The time is ripe.

00:15:05.708 --> 00:15:09.958
Let me give you the gift
of the world's cruelest death.

00:15:09.958 --> 00:15:15.208
Sir... you know who I am, don't you?

00:15:15.208 --> 00:15:19.083
Why don't I reintroduce him--
to your students, too.

00:15:19.083 --> 00:15:24.167
He's the man who stole the name
"the Reaper" from that octopus.

00:15:24.167 --> 00:15:26.125
And...

00:15:28.708 --> 00:15:33.667
...as of today, he's the <i>new </i>Koro Sensei.

00:15:38.875 --> 00:15:42.875
"Assassination Classroom, Final Season"
"by Karma Akabane"

00:15:57.500 --> 00:15:59.375
Farewell, my teacher...

00:15:59.375 --> 00:16:03.208
You never did see my face...

00:16:03.208 --> 00:16:05.125
...did you?

00:16:06.542 --> 00:16:09.375
If there were another with my skills,

00:16:09.375 --> 00:16:12.708
the scope of my assassination work
would widen considerably.

00:16:12.708 --> 00:16:17.333
So when he volunteered to be my pupil,
I took him in and trained him.

00:16:17.333 --> 00:16:19.833
This was a man who admired power.

00:16:19.833 --> 00:16:23.375
And so power he was taught,
just as he'd desired.

00:16:23.375 --> 00:16:29.458
To cultivate loyalty, I showed him
the absolute gap in our power as well.

00:16:29.458 --> 00:16:33.667
I gave him profit and awe in spades.

00:16:33.667 --> 00:16:36.917
There should have been
no element of betrayal.

00:16:39.500 --> 00:16:43.042
Sir! Looking at our
infiltration route for this job,

00:16:43.042 --> 00:16:46.708
aren't there fewer guards
if we come in from the east gate?

00:16:46.708 --> 00:16:50.667
Let me handle this and I'll do all the prepwork!

00:16:50.667 --> 00:16:53.167
Mmm. We won't make any changes.

00:16:53.167 --> 00:16:56.375
Lead us in through here, as planned.

00:16:59.625 --> 00:17:03.500
Sir, I've thought up a knife move
with lots of killing power!

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:07.375
This dual-wield variation--

00:17:07.375 --> 00:17:10.208
Mmm. Doesn't work, does it?

00:17:10.208 --> 00:17:12.667
If you don't want more risk in your work,

00:17:12.667 --> 00:17:15.792
first master the skills you've been taught.

00:17:21.833 --> 00:17:26.125
It's not so much that I was lacking.

00:17:26.125 --> 00:17:30.208
I just didn't understand anything back then.

00:17:30.208 --> 00:17:36.458
Your student probably
just wanted to be seen--by you.

00:17:36.458 --> 00:17:41.458
You were my first student, and I...

00:17:41.458 --> 00:17:44.250
I wasn't seeing you.

00:17:48.625 --> 00:17:50.917
Yanagisawa...

00:17:50.917 --> 00:17:56.125
This showing up now--is that part of your plan?

00:17:56.125 --> 00:18:00.125
So now we can collect actual
combat data <i>and </i>the target's body?

00:18:00.125 --> 00:18:03.792
With just one of <i>those</i>,
the whole war on terror would be over.

00:18:03.792 --> 00:18:06.958
An unkillable, invincible creature...

00:18:06.958 --> 00:18:11.792
I'm sure our nation would
love to put that to practical use.

00:18:12.542 --> 00:18:14.250
That's...

00:18:14.250 --> 00:18:16.000
Is that thing...?

00:18:17.833 --> 00:18:21.792
Reaper 2.0... the one who'd attacked us!

00:18:21.792 --> 00:18:26.792
Before it was just his face--
now his whole body is a monster!

00:18:26.792 --> 00:18:30.625
He's just had the same
modifications as that octopus.

00:18:30.625 --> 00:18:36.833
The only difference is that he begged for them.

00:18:36.833 --> 00:18:42.125
Completely unlike the botched Itona
or my little sister over there.

00:18:42.125 --> 00:18:44.417
Can you even imagine?

00:18:44.417 --> 00:18:48.792
A man who overpowered you
singlehandedly even as a human

00:18:48.792 --> 00:18:51.833
now has both incomparable
tentacles and hatred.

00:18:51.833 --> 00:18:54.375
The destructive power...!

00:18:54.375 --> 00:18:56.417
--Die!
--Run away!

00:19:03.208 --> 00:19:05.000
A sonic boom.

00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:07.917
His tentacles have
an initial velocity of Mach 2.

00:19:07.917 --> 00:19:10.250
And they can reach a top speed...

00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:11.708
...of Mach 40.

00:19:11.708 --> 00:19:13.625
M-Mach 40?!

00:19:13.625 --> 00:19:17.083
In short, his basic performance is doubled.

00:19:17.083 --> 00:19:22.167
2.0's superhuman kinetic vision
and intuition are amplified via his tentacles,

00:19:22.167 --> 00:19:25.917
making him readily adaptable
to a supersonic world.

00:19:25.917 --> 00:19:30.500
Unlike some amateur children,
he took to his tentacles readily--

00:19:30.500 --> 00:19:33.583
just like version 1.0 over there.

00:19:33.583 --> 00:19:35.125
Koro Sensei!

00:19:35.625 --> 00:19:38.708
But the greatest difference
is that unlike you and that octopus,

00:19:38.708 --> 00:19:42.958
those tentacles were designed
with continuous operation in mind.

00:19:42.958 --> 00:19:47.708
You see, he needs no upkeep. He's disposable.

00:19:47.708 --> 00:19:50.208
In exchange for only three months to live,

00:19:50.208 --> 00:19:54.333
I've made it so he can
tap into this tremendous energy.

00:19:54.333 --> 00:19:58.583
And there's not even any danger
of him exploding at death.

00:19:59.875 --> 00:20:02.708
A safe and flawless weapon, is it not?

00:20:02.708 --> 00:20:05.292
You always do this...

00:20:05.292 --> 00:20:07.542
Always hurting others--

00:20:07.542 --> 00:20:10.417
from your safe spot away from it all!

00:20:11.167 --> 00:20:13.667
Is that what you think?

00:20:19.208 --> 00:20:24.625
I'm not prepared to die?
Is that what you think?

00:20:24.625 --> 00:20:26.417
Hey, that's--

00:20:26.417 --> 00:20:27.958
It can't be...

00:20:28.583 --> 00:20:32.958
I don't give a damn about my life anymore.

00:20:32.958 --> 00:20:37.667
Not if I can kill you,
who stole everything from me...

00:20:37.667 --> 00:20:40.750
Joints, muscle fibers, spinal cord, nerves:

00:20:40.750 --> 00:20:43.417
it may not be my entire body,
but if I can gradually implant tentacles

00:20:43.417 --> 00:20:44.917
in these key places,

00:20:44.917 --> 00:20:49.583
I can become superhuman
while retaining my human faculties...

00:20:49.583 --> 00:20:53.042
Die a pathetic death, guinea pig...

00:20:53.042 --> 00:20:57.458
...so your beloved students
will be scarred for life!

00:20:58.417 --> 00:21:00.000
What the--?!

00:21:02.542 --> 00:21:04.917
Class...

00:21:04.917 --> 00:21:09.875
There's something I forgot
to mention in my earlier lesson:

00:21:09.875 --> 00:21:14.333
Even an assassin who's cleverly
avoided all head-to-head battles

00:21:14.333 --> 00:21:17.125
is sure to have a number of times in life

00:21:17.125 --> 00:21:21.458
when he or she must fight
with every last ounce of strength.

00:21:22.500 --> 00:21:25.292
In my case...

00:21:25.292 --> 00:21:27.583
...that would be now!

00:21:32.583 --> 00:21:44.583
<i>In the big window where</i>
<i>the dappled sunlight shines gently in</i>

00:21:44.583 --> 00:21:56.542
<i>The day I met you felt so far away</i>

00:21:56.542 --> 00:22:07.500
<i>The memories I've arranged</i>
<i>little by little keep me warm</i>

00:22:07.500 --> 00:22:19.042
<i>A small room, hearts connecting:</i>
<i>you taught me gently</i>

00:22:19.042 --> 00:22:31.792
<i>Once this season comes for me, I won't be able</i>

00:22:31.792 --> 00:22:37.042
<i>To search out your figure anymore</i>

00:22:37.042 --> 00:22:42.792
<i>I'll never forget</i>

00:22:42.792 --> 00:23:02.059
<i>Until the day I can see you again</i>
